    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-backgrounds-and-backgroundbased-bonus-feats",
      "heading": "Backgrounds and Background-Based Bonus Feats",
      "sourceAnchor": "backgrounds-and-backgroundbased-bonus-feats",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-backgrounds-and-backgroundbased-bonus-feats-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Glory of the Giants introduces two new backgrounds. One provides the Runeshaper feat, while the other provides the Strike of the Giants feat. The book suggests granting players their choice of Skilled or Tough if the DM chooses to allow the new backgrounds, which gives us a balance point against which to compare Runeshaper and Strike of the Giants."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-backgrounds-and-backgroundbased-bonus-feats-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In short: Runeshaper and Strike of the Giants should be roughly as useful as Skilled or Tough."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-backgrounds-and-backgroundbased-bonus-feats-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The thing that makes the Dragonlance backgrounds immediately so powerful is that, because it doesn’t say you can’t, we can assume that you can use all the typical rules for customizing backgrounds available to the rest of them. This means that it’s basically just “this feat for free on top of whatever regular background stuff you want.” You’re free to keep the background’s Feature (feats in this case) but rearrange the proficiencies. This means that reviewing the backgrounds individually is somewhat pointless."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-backgrounds-and-backgroundbased-bonus-feats-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An interesting piece of this is that the backgrounds are also prerequisites for the feats, allowing you to bypass the other prerequisites for Rune Shaper and for Strike of the Giants."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-features",
      "heading": "Rune Shaper",
      "sourceAnchor": "features",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-features-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You learn Comprehend Languages and can cast it for free once per day, but the primary appeal here is the runes. You get 1 to 3 runes per day based on your Proficiency Bonus, and each rune lets you temporarily know a single 1st-level spell and cast it once per day for free."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-features-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The runes allow you to select spells not on your class’s spell list, giving us options like Armor of Agathys on a gish build without taking a warlock class dip."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-features-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "They can also expand your pool of spells known, which can be helpful for classes like the Bard and the Sorcerer, who get a strictly limited number of spells known. You might weigh that benefit against "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "spellcasting feats",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/feats/spellcasting-feats/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " like Fey Touched, but remember that Runeshaper is expected to be in line with Skilled or Tough, which aren’t stunning powerful feats."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-features-4",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Cloud"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A decent escape mechanism, but\n\t\tmost parties won’t use it often enough to bring it every day."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Death"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Among the best damage options from\n\t\t1st-level spells, but remember that it’s melee range and the spell scaling\n\t\tis poor, so you’ll likely replace it as you gain levels."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Dragon"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Among the best damage options\n\t\tfrom 1st-level spells, but the spell scaling is poor, so you’ll likely\n\t\treplace it as you gain levels."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Enemy"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Only situationally useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Fire"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Passable area damage at low\n\t\tlevels, but obsolete quickly due to the tiny area of effect."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Friend"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Only situationally useful and\n\t\tit’s difficult to predict."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Frost"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": An amazing buff for melee casters\n\t\tof all kinds. Usually this takes a warlock dip to get."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Hill"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A decent way to turn leftover\n\t\tspell slots into some healing for the next day. Especially appealing for\n\t\tlife clerics who were eyeing a druid dip."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Journey"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A helpful buff with a nice long\n\t\tduration. Not always impactful, but still great for melee characters."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "King"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Decent crowd control and the\n\t\tscaling is decent."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Mountain"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good area control for such a\n\t\tlow-level spell, but it might become obsolete as you gain levels and flight\n\t\tbecomes increasingly common."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Stone"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A great defensive option at any\n\t\tlevel."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Storm"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Short range, poor damage, and\n\t\tit’s on a Constitution save."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
