        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ember-of-the-fire-giant",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strike-of-the-giants",
      "heading": "Ember of the Fire Giant",
      "sourceAnchor": "ember-of-the-fire-giant",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ember-of-the-fire-giant-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A +1 ability score increase, fire resistance and an AOE burst which blinds nearby enemies in place of one of your attacks. The damage is minor, but makes up for the damage that your attack might have done. Blinding enemies in the radius means that you could debuff multiple enemies, then spend the rest of your turn attacking them with Advantage. The effect ends at the beginning of your next turn, but your allies all get a round to capitalize on your enemies being blind."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fury-of-the-frost-giant",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strike-of-the-giants",
      "heading": "Fury of the Frost Giant",
      "sourceAnchor": "fury-of-the-frost-giant",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fury-of-the-frost-giant-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A +1 ability score increase, cold resistance, and a Reaction similar to Hellish Rebuke. The Reaction targets Constitution saves, and Constitution saves tend to be high, so this may not be reliable."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-guile-of-the-cloud-giant",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strike-of-the-giants",
      "heading": "Guile of the Cloud Giant",
      "sourceAnchor": "guile-of-the-cloud-giant",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-guile-of-the-cloud-giant-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A +1 ability score increase, and a Reaction to teleport and reduce damage when you’re hit by an attack. This can mitigate a huge amount of damage over the course of a day, the teleportation is a great way to get out of dangerous spaces or grapples, and you may be able to teleport to somewhere to prevent your attacker from making further attacks. "
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-keenness-of-the-stone-giant",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strike-of-the-giants",
      "heading": "Keenness of the Stone Giant",
      "sourceAnchor": "keenness-of-the-stone-giant",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-keenness-of-the-stone-giant-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A +1 ability score increase, Darkvision, and you can throw a stone as a Bonus Action a few times per day. The damage is pitiful (1d10 and no ability score modifier), but the stone’s biggest appeal is knocking your target prone, but it’s only notable compared to Strike of the Giants (Stone) because you can do it as a Bonus Action. I’m not sure if that’s worth the feat."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-soul-of-the-storm-giant",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strike-of-the-giants",
      "heading": "Soul of the Storm Giant",
      "sourceAnchor": "soul-of-the-storm-giant",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-soul-of-the-storm-giant-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Give yourself a personal Fog Cloud for a turn. The Disadvantage effect is great if you’re drawing a lot of attention and need some short-term protection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-soul-of-the-storm-giant-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The speed debuff is neat and could keep enemies from moving out of your reach, which can be helpful for a Defender. However, at PB/day uses you won’t be able to use this enough to build your tactics around it, so you still want things like Sentinel."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-vigor-of-the-hill-giant",
      "parentSectionId": "section-strike-of-the-giants",
      "heading": "Vigor of the Hill Giant",
      "sourceAnchor": "vigor-of-the-hill-giant",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vigor-of-the-hill-giant-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "+1 ability score increase and you get some extra hp when you take a Short Rest. I wouldn’t consider this on anyone except a barbarian who was chronically short on hit points. Even then, Guile of the Cloud Giant can prevent more damage in a day than this will heal."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
